{# THE WALL ITSELF — twenty-four hours across, one post per row, a block for
   every watch and a line where now is.

   IT IS A PARTIAL BECAUSE TWO SURFACES DRAW IT: the Day board tab and the
   dashboard's day-board widget. The library's preview IS the widget, so the
   picture and the page have to be one file or they drift.

   A NIGHT WATCH IS TWO BLOCKS. It crosses midnight, so the morning before
   06:00 belongs to the watch that began yesterday; drawing it as one would
   be a lie about the day it belongs to. #}
    <div class="r-day">
        <div class="r-ruler">
            <span></span>
            <span class="hrs">{% for hour in [0, 3, 6, 9, 12, 15, 18, 21] %}<span>{{ '%02d'|format(hour) }}</span>{% endfor %}</span>
        </div>
        <div class="r-daywrap">
            {% for post in posts %}
                <div class="r-dayrow">
                    <span class="lbl">{{ post.stationName }}<em>{{ post.state.label }}</em></span>
                    <span class="r-track">
                        {%- for block in blocks[post.stationUuid]|default([]) %}
                            <span class="r-blk{{ block.crossesMidnight ? ' night' : '' }}"
                                  style="left:{{ block.leftPercent }}%;width:{{ block.widthPercent }}%"
                                  title="{{ block.label }}{{ block.fromYesterday ? ' — began yesterday' : '' }}: {{ block.people|join(' · ') }}">
                                <span class="n">{{ block.count }}</span> {{ block.people|join(' · ') }}
                            </span>
                        {%- else %}
                            <span class="r-blk gap" style="left:0;width:100%">
                                {{ post.state.value == 'no_watch' ? 'no watch declared — never counted, never late, never a hole' : 'nothing rostered on this day' }}
                            </span>
                        {%- endfor %}
                    </span>
                </div>
            {% endfor %}
            {# WHERE NOW IS, PLACED BY THE VIEWER'S OWN CLOCK.

               The server renders the DAY and nothing else. It cannot place
               this line: the ruling is that the viewer's clock is the
               authority for every instant, a server-rendered percent is in
               the server's timezone, and — the defect somebody actually
               reported — it is frozen at render, so on the office-wall
               screen this board is built for it stops moving the moment the
               page loads. The controller places it from the browser's clock
               and again on every minute boundary, and hides it outright on
               a day that is not the viewer's today. #}
            <div class="r-now" hidden
                 data-controller="roster--now-line"
                 data-roster--now-line-day-value="{{ day.format('Y-m-d') }}"></div>
        </div>
